🔹 ... (Triple dots) — Rest aur Spread dono mein use hota hai, lekin context alag hota hai.
✅ 1. Rest Operator
Jab hum unknown ya baaki values ko collect karte hain.

Mostly function parameters ya destructuring mein use hota hai.

📌 Example (Function mein):
javascript

function sum(...nums) {
  return nums.reduce((acc, val) => acc + val, 0);
}
console.log(sum(1, 2, 3)); // 6
Explanation: ...nums saare arguments ko ek array bana deta hai.

📌 Example (Destructuring mein):
javascript

const [a, ...rest] = [1, 2, 3, 4];
console.log(rest); // [2, 3, 4]
✅ 2. Spread Operator
Jab hum values ko expand karte hain (array ya object ke andar).

Mostly copying, merging, ya function arguments mein use hota hai.

📌 Example (Array Copy):
javascript

const arr1 = [1, 2];
const arr2 = [...arr1, 3, 4];
console.log(arr2); // [1, 2, 3, 4]
📌 Example (Object Copy):
javascript

const obj1 = { name: "Vinayak" };
const obj2 = { ...obj1, age: 25 };
console.log(obj2); // { name: "Vinayak", age: 25 }
🔁 Summary:
Use	Operator	Purpose
Rest	...	Collect remaining values into array
Spread	...	Expand elements of array/object

