Great! Yahaan par maine Rest aur Spread Operators ke real-world examples diye hain — simple Hinglish mein, with code:

✅ 1. REST Operator – React Props ke saath
React component mein, jab hume kuch props alag se chahiye aur baaki sab collect karne ho:

jsx

function Button({ label, ...props }) {
  return <button {...props}>{label}</button>;
}

// Use
<Button label="Click Me" onClick={handleClick} className="btn" />
Explanation:

label directly le liya.

...props mein baaki sab (onClick, className) aa gaya.

Spread ki help se button ke andar pass kiya.

✅ 2. SPREAD Operator – Array Merge ya Copy
🔹 Combine product lists from two APIs:
javascript

const amazonProducts = ["TV", "Mobile"];
const flipkartProducts = ["Laptop", "Tablet"];

const allProducts = [...amazonProducts, ...flipkartProducts];
console.log(allProducts); // ['TV', 'Mobile', 'Laptop', 'Tablet']
✅ 3. REST in Function Parameters (Dynamic Inputs)
javascript

function logMessages(type, ...messages) {
  messages.forEach(msg => console.log(`[${type}] ${msg}`));
}

logMessages("ERROR", "Server down", "Timeout", "Connection failed");
Output:

csharp

[ERROR] Server down  
[ERROR] Timeout  
[ERROR] Connection failed
✅ 4. SPREAD in State Updates (React – immutability)
javascript

const [user, setUser] = useState({ name: "Vinayak", age: 25 });

const updateAge = () => {
  setUser(prev => ({ ...prev, age: 26 }));
};
Explanation:

...prev copies existing data.

Only age update hota hai, baaki safe rehta hai.

✅ 5. REST in Object Destructuring
javascript

const person = { name: "Vinayak", age: 25, country: "India" };
const { name, ...otherDetails } = person;

console.log(name); // Vinayak
console.log(otherDetails); // { age: 25, country: 'India' }
